From 219c608552e46df4a686613ece8e43f06e2ef7aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:20:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: banners arrive top centre, the tray opens on its
 beacon, cards fit

Banners now arrive at the top centre of the active monitor by default,
centred in what the Shelf leaves free and dropping in from the top edge;
the corners remain choices. Do Not Disturb and Cast's silenced and captured
monitors are unchanged.

The notification tray opened at the far right of the screen whatever was
clicked. It now opens 8 beyond the island of the item that opened it,
centred on that item and kept wholly on that item's monitor (placement is
pure and tested, including a 5120px ultrawide beside a scaled laptop), or
beside the item on a side Shelf.

With many notifications the tray's cards overlapped: the list is a
viewport, a viewport gives its children their minimum heights before it
scrolls, and a card's minimum was only its first line, so every two-line
preview was drawn over the next card and nothing scrolled. A tray card's
minimum is now its natural height, so cards keep their previews (two lines,
ellipsized) and the list scrolls. The header lines up with the cards.

The beacon said its count twice -- "Discord and 13 more" beside a "14" on a
brown blob taken from the application's tone. It now names the newest
notification's application, and the count is the kit's count chip: a 24px
capsule on the island's hover fill with ink tabular numerals, shown from two
notifications.

A card's soft shadow was bound to the card with a constraint that kept the
size and place the card first measured at, so once the stack moved a card
a dark band trailed across the screen from where it had been. The frame's
bin now gives the shadow the card's own box.
